# A hint that names a terminal written by name and decides nothing says
# which terminal: `"(" (LPAREN)`.
# error: x_hint_dead_named.grammar:19:10:
# error: X "(" on name → IDENT has no effect: it decides no shift/reduce conflict between this rule and "(" (LPAREN); remove the hint
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    lparen
    rparen
    eof
    err
'\n'                                        → skip, skip
'('                                         → lparen
')'                                         → rparen
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
call!  = name LPAREN RPAREN                 → (call 1)
name   = IDENT X "("                        → 1
